/// Single switch for recording the demo video without a configured
/// Firebase project.
///
/// When true: no Firebase init, no real auth, no Firestore — the app
/// runs entirely on an in-memory [CaseStore] pre-loaded with sample
/// cases (see `CaseStore.demo()`), so every screen is fully interactive
/// (filing a case, pleading, jury voting, automatic verdicts) with
/// nothing to set up.
///
/// Flip to false once `lib/firebase_options.dart` exists (generated by
/// `flutterfire configure`) and Firebase Auth/Firestore are turned on —
/// nothing else in the app needs to change.
const bool kDemoMode = true;
